{title: Blest Be the Tie That Binds}
{artist: John Fawcett}
{key: F}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[F]Blest be the [Bb]tie that [F]binds our [Bb]hearts in [C]Christian [F]love:
the fellowship of [Bb]kindred [F]minds is [Bb]like to [C]that a[F]bove.

Verse 2
[F]Before our Father's [Bb]throne We [F]pour our ardent [Bb]prayers; Our [C]fears, [F]our
hopes, our aims [Bb]are [F]one Our [Bb]comforts and [C]our cares.

Verse 3
[F]We share [Bb]each other's [F]woes, Our [Bb]mutual [C]burdens [F]bear;
And often for [Bb]each [F]other [Bb]flows The [C]sympathizing tear.

Verse 4
[F]When we asunder [Bb]part, It [F]gives us inward [Bb]pain; But [C]we [F]shall
still be joined [Bb]in [F]heart, And [Bb]hope to [C]meet again.

Verse 5
[F]This glorious hope [Bb]revives Our [F]courage [Bb]by the [C]way; [F]While
each in expectation [Bb]lives, [F]And longs [Bb]to see [C]the day.
